  "assembly": "# Advent of Code 2025, day 6 part 2 (Trash Compactor)\n#\n# THE PUZZLE\n# The input is a worksheet of problems side by side: digits in the upper rows and a + or * in the last\n# row under each problem's first column. In part 2 a number is written downwards: each column of\n# characters is one number, its top digit the most significant. A problem's numbers are added or\n# multiplied, as its sign says, and a column of only spaces separates two problems. The answer is the\n# sum of all the problems' results.\n#\n# THE IDEA\n# The worksheet is in memory character by character, row after row, so the character below a character\n# is STRIDE = (characters per row) + 1 words further on. The program reads it one column at a time from\n# the left (the order of the numbers does not matter for a sum or a product):\n#     - a sign under the column: a new problem starts. VALUE = 0 for +, 1 for *.\n#     - the column's digits, read downwards, make the number N: N = N * 10 + digit.\n#     - a column with digits: VALUE = VALUE + N, or VALUE = VALUE * N.\n#     - a column without digits: the problem is finished. TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE.\n# The example's first problem:     1 2 3      column 1: sign *, VALUE = 1; N = 1;   VALUE = 1\n#                                    4 5      column 2: N = 24;                     VALUE = 24\n#                                      6      column 3: N = 356;                    VALUE = 8544\n#                                  *          column 4: no digits: TOTAL = TOTAL + 8544\n#\n# MULTIPLYING WITHOUT A MULTIPLY INSTRUCTION\n# N * 10 is N * 8 + N * 2, two shifts and a sum. VALUE * N is done as on paper, but in binary: N is a sum\n# of powers of two, and VALUE * N is the sum of VALUE * (those powers). VALUE * 2 is VALUE + VALUE. For\n# 123 * 5 (5 = 4 + 1):\n#     BIT = 1    5 has the 1    RESULT = 0 + 123 = 123       VALUE = 123 + 123 = 246\n#     BIT = 2    5 has no 2                                  VALUE = 246 + 246 = 492\n#     BIT = 4    5 has the 4    RESULT = 123 + 492 = 615     VALUE = 984\n#     BIT = 8    8 > 5: finished, 123 * 5 = 615\n# \"N has the BIT\" is (N and BIT) != 0. A number of four digits takes at most 14 rounds.\n#\n# THE WHOLE PROGRAM IN PSEUDO CODE\n#     STRIDE = (address of the first row's end mark) - GRID + 1\n#     SIGN = GRID; while memory[SIGN] < 0xFFF1: SIGN = SIGN + STRIDE     # the row of signs\n#     TOTAL = 0; VALUE = 0; C = GRID\n#     while memory[C] != END_MARK:                          # one column of characters\n#         if memory[SIGN] != BLANK:                         # a new problem\n#             OP = memory[SIGN]\n#             VALUE = 1 if OP == TIMES else 0\n#         N = 0; SEEN = 0\n#         for P = C; P != SIGN; P = P + STRIDE:             # down the column\n#             if memory[P] != BLANK: N = N * 10 + memory[P]; SEEN = 1\n#         if SEEN == 0: TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; VALUE = 0    # the column between two problems\n#         else if OP == TIMES: VALUE = VALUE * N\n#         else: VALUE = VALUE + N\n#         C = C + 1; SIGN = SIGN + 1\n#     TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE                                 # the last problem has no column after it\n#     write TOTAL as 15 decimal digits\n#     stop\n#\n# NUMBERS OF FOUR WORDS\n# A product of four numbers of four digits needs up to 54 bits, more than the 32 bits of a register. So\n# TOTAL, VALUE and RESULT are four 16-bit words each, lowest word first: VALUE is the words VALUE0\n# (lowest) to VALUE3 (top). N is one word.\n#   Adding: word by word from the lowest. Two words are added in a 32-bit register; the lower half of\n#     the sum is the result's word, the upper half is the carry into the next word.\n#   Subtracting (only for the decimal digits): the CPU cannot borrow from one word to the next, so X - Y\n#     is X + (every bit of Y flipped) + 1. The carry out of the top word is 1 exactly when X >= Y.\n#\n# THE RESULT, when the CPU stops on the Breakpoint at END\n#   0x0100-0x0103  TOTAL as four 16-bit words, lowest first\n#   0x0110-0x011E  TOTAL as 15 decimal digits, one per word, most significant first\n#\n# THE INPUT (rule 1 of RULES.md), at 0x2000\n# The worksheet row by row, one word per character: a digit is its value (0 to 9), a space is 0xFFF0,\n# + is 0xFFF1, * is 0xFFF2. Every row, the row of signs too, is followed by the end mark 0xFFFF.\n# Built-in limits: every row has the same count of characters; the first column holds a sign; there is\n# at least one row of digits; every number is below 32,768 (four digits always are); every result\n# and the answer are below 2^64, and the answer below 10^15.\n#\n# THE IDIOMS (v is a variable's address, below 0x1000)\n#     getA v                   A = the word at v   (lia v; load rgA rgA: lia puts the address in A, load replaces it)\n#     getB v                   B = the word at v\n#     putA v                   the word at v = A   (this uses up B)\n#     getAat p / putAat p      the same for the word the pointer p points at\n#     copy v w                 w = v\n#     getAoff p k              A = the word at the address (p + k); p is a variable holding an address\n#     keepcarry v              v = the upper half of A: the carry of the sum just made\n#     if_eq L / if_neq L       compares A with B as they are now\n#     sub; if_carry L          after A - B: taken when A >= B\n# What each instruction does exactly is in findings/cpu-instructions.md.\n#\n# MEMORY MAP\n#   0x0100-0x0155  variables            0x1E00-  POWERS: 10^14 down to 1, four words each, then 0\n#   0x1000-        the program          0x2000-  the worksheet (4 rows of 3730 characters and the signs end at 0x68DE)\n#   0x1800-        the subroutines      0xFF00   where the CPU starts\n\n# ---- The CPU's instructions as symbols (day 1's table without its _32 names, which the CPU ignores) ----\nsymbol nop 0b0000_0000_0000_0000            # the word 0: stops the CPU (the same word as non)\nsymbol ld  0b0010_0000_0000_0000            # load a register from memory (used through the load macro)\nsymbol lia 0b0011_0000_0000_0000            # lia n: A = n (0 to 4095), upper half 0\nsymbol lib 0b0100_0000_0000_0000            # lib n: B = n (0 to 4095), upper half 0\nsymbol sto 0b0101_0000_0000_0000            # store a register to memory (used through the store macro)\n\nmacro  load  { ld  | a? | (b? >> 6) }       # load X Y: X = the word at the address in Y\nmacro  store { sto | a? | (b? >> 6) }       # store X Y: the word at the address in Y = X\n\nsymbol sum    0b0110_0100_0000_0000         # A = A + B (32 bits), sets zero, carry, nega\nsymbol sub    0b0110_0010_0000_0000         # A = A - B (32 bits), sets zero, carry, nega\nsymbol shf    0b0110_0001_0000_0000         # shf | k: A = A shifted left by k (0 to 15)\nsymbol and    0b0110_0000_1000_0000         # A = A and B\nsymbol or     0b0110_0000_0100_0000         # A = A or B\nsymbol xor    0b0110_0000_0010_0000         # A = A xor B\nsymbol neg    0b0110_0000_0001_0000         # A = every bit of A flipped\n\nsymbol psh 0b1010_0000_0000_0000            # psh X: push the 16 bits of X\nsymbol pop 0b1011_0000_0000_0000            # pop X: pop 16 bits into X\n\nsymbol jmp  0b1100_0000_0000_0000           # jmp; L: go to L.  jmp c; L: go to L when c holds\nsymbol call 0b1110_0000_0000_0000           # call; L: run the subroutine at L\nsymbol ret  0b1111_0000_0000_0000           # return from a subroutine\n\n# The registers, as load, store, psh and pop name them\nsymbol rgAH 0b1000_0000_0000                # the upper 16 bits of A\nsymbol rgA  0b0100_0000_0000                # the lower 16 bits of A\nsymbol rgBH 0b0010_0000_0000                # the upper 16 bits of B\nsymbol rgB  0b0001_0000_0000                # the lower 16 bits of B\nsymbol rgSP 0b0000_1000_0000                # the program counter (leave alone)\nsymbol rgSB 0b0000_0100_0000                # the stack pointer (leave alone)\nsymbol non  0                               # stops the CPU (Breakpoint): the end of the program\n\n# The conditions of jmp\nsymbol zero  0b1000_0000_0000               # the last sum or sub gave 0\nsymbol carry 0b0100_0000_0000               # the last sum carried, or the last sub did not borrow (A >= B)\nsymbol nega  0b0010_0000_0000               # the last sub went below 0 (A < B)\nsymbol eq    0b0001_0000_0000               # A == B right now\nsymbol neq   0b0000_1000_0000               # A != B right now\n\n# ---- Macros for the common operations (explained in the README). A macro cannot use another macro, so\n#      load and store are spelled out here. v: a variable, p: a variable holding an address, L: a label ----\nmacro getA     { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                                              # A = v\nmacro getB     { lib a?; ld | rgB | (rgB >> 6) }                                              # B = v\nmacro putA     { lib a?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                                             # v = A (uses B)\nmacro getAat   { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                       # A = the word p points at\nmacro putAat   { lib a?; ld | rgB | (rgB >> 6); sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                      # the word p points at = A (uses B)\nmacro inc      { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib 1; sum; lib a?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }  # v = v + 1 (uses A and B)\nmacro goto     { jmp; a? }                                                                    # go to L\nmacro if_eq    { jmp eq; a? }                                                                 # go to L when A == B\nmacro do       { call; a? }                                                                   # call the subroutine L\nmacro if_carry { jmp carry; a? }                                                              # go to L after a sub when A >= B\nmacro getAoff  { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib b?; sum; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6) }                # A = the word at (p + k) (uses B)\nmacro copy     { lia a?; ld | rgA | (rgA >> 6); lib b?; sto | rgA | (rgB >> 6) }                      # w = v (uses A and B)\nmacro keepcarry { psh rgAH; pop rgB; lia a?; sto | rgB | (rgA >> 6) }                                 # v = the upper half of A (uses A and B)\nmacro if_neq   { jmp neq; a? }                                                                # go to L when A != B\n\n\n# ---- Variables (all below 0x1000, so lia/lib can address them). A number is four words, 0 the lowest ----\n# The result: the sum of the problems so far\npointer TOTAL0 0x0100 0\npointer TOTAL1 0x0101 0\npointer TOTAL2 0x0102 0\npointer TOTAL3 0x0103 0\n# VALUE: the problem's sum or product so far. In MULTIPLY it is doubled round by round\npointer VALUE0 0x0120 0\npointer VALUE1 0x0121 0\npointer VALUE2 0x0122 0\npointer VALUE3 0x0123 0\n# RESULT: what MULTIPLY has added up\npointer RESULT0 0x0124 0\npointer RESULT1 0x0125 0\npointer RESULT2 0x0126 0\npointer RESULT3 0x0127 0\n# SUBTRACT works out DIFF = X - Y (for the decimal digits)\npointer X0 0x0128 0\npointer X1 0x0129 0\npointer X2 0x012A 0\npointer X3 0x012B 0\npointer Y0 0x012C 0\npointer Y1 0x012D 0\npointer Y2 0x012E 0\npointer Y3 0x012F 0\npointer DIFF0 0x0130 0\npointer DIFF1 0x0131 0\npointer DIFF2 0x0132 0\npointer DIFF3 0x0133 0\n# The carry from one word of an addition into the next\npointer CARRY 0x0138 0\n# N: the number in the column. SEEN: 1 when the column held a digit. BIT: the power of two MULTIPLY is looking at\npointer N 0x0139 0\npointer SEEN 0x013A 0\npointer BIT 0x013B 0\n# OP: the sign of the problem being read. TWICE: N * 2 while N * 10 is worked out. D: the digit just read\npointer OP 0x013C 0\npointer TWICE 0x013D 0\npointer D 0x013E 0\n# C: the address of the column's character in the first row. SIGN: the address of the character under the column\n# in the row of signs. P walks from C down to SIGN\npointer C 0x0140 0x2000\npointer SIGN 0x0141 0x2000\npointer P 0x0142 0\n# STRIDE: the distance from a character to the one below it\npointer STRIDE 0x0143 0\n# For the decimal digits: how often the current power of ten fitted\npointer DIGIT_VALUE 0x0144 0\n# Pointers: DIGIT the next digit to write, POW the next power of ten\npointer DIGIT 0x0145 0x0110\npointer POW 0x0146 0x1E00\n# Constants that do not fit an instruction's place for a number\npointer GRID 0x0150 0x2000\npointer END_MARK 0x0151 0xFFFF\npointer BLANK 0x0152 0xFFF0\npointer FIRST_SIGN 0x0153 0xFFF1\npointer TIMES 0x0154 0xFFF2\npointer ALL_ONES 0x0155 0xFFFF\n\n# ---- The CPU starts at 0xFF00 ----\norigin 0xFF00\ngoto MAIN\n\norigin 0x1000\n@ MAIN\n# ==== find the length of a row ====\n#     P = GRID\n#     while memory[P] != END_MARK: P = P + 1        # P is free for this; it walks along the first row\n#     STRIDE = P - GRID + 1\n@ FIND_WIDTH\n\tgetA GRID; putA P                                            # P = the address of the worksheet\n@ FIND_WIDTH_NEXT\n\tgetAat P; getB END_MARK                                      # A = memory[P], B = the end mark\n\tif_eq WIDTH_FOUND                                            # the first row's end mark\n\tinc P                                                        # P = P + 1\n\tgoto FIND_WIDTH_NEXT\n@ WIDTH_FOUND\n\tgetA P; getB GRID; sub                                       # A = P - GRID, the count of characters in a row\n\tlib 1; sum; putA STRIDE                                      # STRIDE = that + 1\n\n# ==== find the row of signs ====\n#     while memory[SIGN] < 0xFFF1: SIGN = SIGN + STRIDE     # SIGN starts at GRID; the first column holds a sign\n@ FIND_SIGNS\n\tgetAat SIGN; getB FIRST_SIGN; sub                            # A = memory[SIGN] - 0xFFF1\n\tif_carry NEXT_COLUMN                                         # not below 0xFFF1: a sign, so this is the row of signs\n\tgetA SIGN; getB STRIDE; sum; putA SIGN                       # SIGN = SIGN + STRIDE, the row below\n\tgoto FIND_SIGNS\n\n# ==== one column: does a problem start here? ====\n#     if memory[C] == END_MARK: goto ALL_COLUMNS_DONE\n#     if memory[SIGN] != BLANK:\n#         OP = memory[SIGN]\n#         VALUE = 1 if OP == TIMES else 0\n@ NEXT_COLUMN\n\tgetAat C; getB END_MARK                                      # A = memory[C], B = the end mark\n\tif_eq ALL_COLUMNS_DONE                                       # the end of the first row: no more columns\n\tgetAat SIGN; getB BLANK                                      # A = the character under the column, B = a space\n\tif_eq READ_NUMBER                                            # no sign: the same problem goes on\n\tputA OP                                                      # OP = the sign\n\tlia 0; putA VALUE0; putA VALUE1; putA VALUE2; putA VALUE3    # VALUE = 0, all four words\n\tgetA OP; getB TIMES                                          # A = OP, B = the sign *\n\tif_neq READ_NUMBER                                           # a + problem starts at 0\n\tlia 1; putA VALUE0                                           # a * problem starts at 1\n\n# ==== read the number in the column ====\n#     N = 0; SEEN = 0\n#     for P = C; P != SIGN; P = P + STRIDE:\n#         if memory[P] != BLANK:\n#             N = N * 10 + memory[P]                # N * 10 = N * 2 + N * 8\n#             SEEN = 1\n@ READ_NUMBER\n\tlia 0; putA N; putA SEEN                                     # N = 0; SEEN = 0\n\tcopy C P                                                     # P = C, the top of the column\n@ READ_DIGIT\n\tgetA P; getB SIGN                                            # A = P, B = SIGN\n\tif_eq NUMBER_READ                                            # P has reached the row of signs\n\tgetAat P; getB BLANK                                         # A = memory[P], B = a space\n\tif_eq DIGIT_DONE                                             # no digit in this row\n\tputA D                                                       # D = the digit\n\tgetA N; shf | 1; putA TWICE                                  # TWICE = N * 2\n\tgetA N; shf | 3                                              # A = N * 8\n\tgetB TWICE; sum                                              # A = N * 8 + N * 2 = N * 10\n\tgetB D; sum; putA N                                          # N = N * 10 + D\n\tlia 1; putA SEEN                                             # SEEN = 1\n@ DIGIT_DONE\n\tgetA P; getB STRIDE; sum; putA P                             # P = P + STRIDE, the character below\n\tgoto READ_DIGIT\n\n# ==== use the number ====\n#     if SEEN == 0: ADD_VALUE                       # TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; VALUE = 0\n#     else if OP == TIMES: MULTIPLY                 # VALUE = VALUE * N\n#     else: VALUE = VALUE + N\n#     C = C + 1; SIGN = SIGN + 1\n@ NUMBER_READ\n\tgetA SEEN; lib 0                                             # A = SEEN, B = 0\n\tif_eq PROBLEM_DONE                                           # a column without digits: the problem is finished\n\tgetA OP; getB TIMES                                          # A = OP, B = the sign *\n\tif_eq TIMES_NUMBER\n\tlia 0; putA CARRY                                            # CARRY = 0\n\tgetA VALUE0; getB N; sum; putA VALUE0; keepcarry CARRY       # VALUE = VALUE + N; word 0: VALUE0 = VALUE0 + N\n\tgetA VALUE1; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE1; keepcarry CARRY   # word 1: VALUE1 = VALUE1 + carry\n\tgetA VALUE2; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE2; keepcarry CARRY   # word 2\n\tgetA VALUE3; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE3                    # word 3 (the top)\n\tgoto COLUMN_DONE\n@ TIMES_NUMBER\n\tdo MULTIPLY                                                  # VALUE = VALUE * N\n\tgoto COLUMN_DONE\n@ PROBLEM_DONE\n\tdo ADD_VALUE                                                 # TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; VALUE = 0\n@ COLUMN_DONE\n\tinc C                                                        # C = C + 1\n\tinc SIGN                                                     # SIGN = SIGN + 1\n\tgoto NEXT_COLUMN\n\n# ==== the last problem has no empty column after it ====\n#     ADD_VALUE                                     # adds 0 when the worksheet ends in a column of spaces\n@ ALL_COLUMNS_DONE\n\tdo ADD_VALUE                                                 # TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; VALUE = 0\n\n# ==== write TOTAL as 15 decimal digits ====\n# A digit is how often a power of ten fits into what is left. Without division that is counting.\n# X is what is left of the total, Y the power of ten:\n#     X = TOTAL\n#     for Y in 10^14, 10^13, ..., 10, 1:                # the table ends at a number whose lowest word is 0\n#         DIGIT_VALUE = 0\n#         loop:\n#             SUBTRACT                                  # DIFF = X - Y, CARRY = 1 when X >= Y\n#             if CARRY == 0: break\n#             X = DIFF; DIGIT_VALUE = DIGIT_VALUE + 1\n#         memory[DIGIT] = DIGIT_VALUE; DIGIT = DIGIT + 1\n# (The lowest word of a power of ten up to 10^15 is never 0, so a 0 there can end the table.)\n@ WRITE_TOTAL\n\tcopy TOTAL0 X0                                               # X = TOTAL; word 0 (the lowest)\n\tcopy TOTAL1 X1                                               # word 1\n\tcopy TOTAL2 X2                                               # word 2\n\tcopy TOTAL3 X3                                               # word 3 (the top)\n@ NEXT_POWER\n\tgetAat POW                                                   # A = the lowest word of the next power of ten\n\tlib 0                                                        # B = 0\n\tif_eq END                                                    # a lowest word of 0 ends the table\n\tputA Y0                                                      # Y = the power of ten; word 0 (the lowest)\n\tgetAoff POW 1; putA Y1                                       # word 1\n\tgetAoff POW 2; putA Y2                                       # word 2\n\tgetAoff POW 3; putA Y3                                       # word 3 (the top)\n\tgetA POW; lib 4; sum; putA POW                               # POW = POW + 4\n\tlia 0; putA DIGIT_VALUE                                      # DIGIT_VALUE = 0\n@ FITS_AGAIN\n\tdo SUBTRACT                                                  # DIFF = X - Y, CARRY = 1 when X >= Y\n\tgetA CARRY; lib 0                                            # A = CARRY, B = 0\n\tif_eq WRITE_DIGIT                                            # X < Y: the power does not fit again\n\tcopy DIFF0 X0                                                # X = DIFF; word 0 (the lowest)\n\tcopy DIFF1 X1                                                # word 1\n\tcopy DIFF2 X2                                                # word 2\n\tcopy DIFF3 X3                                                # word 3 (the top)\n\tinc DIGIT_VALUE                                              # DIGIT_VALUE = DIGIT_VALUE + 1\n\tgoto FITS_AGAIN\n@ WRITE_DIGIT\n\tgetA DIGIT_VALUE; putAat DIGIT                               # memory[DIGIT] = DIGIT_VALUE\n\tinc DIGIT                                                    # DIGIT = DIGIT + 1\n\tgoto NEXT_POWER\n\n# The word 0 stops the CPU on its Breakpoint.\n@ END\n\tnon\n\n# ---- Subroutines ----\norigin 0x1800\n# ADD_VALUE: a problem is finished.\n#     TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; VALUE = 0\n@ ADD_VALUE\n\tlia 0; putA CARRY                                            # CARRY = 0\n\tgetA TOTAL0; getB VALUE0; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA TOTAL0; keepcarry CARRY # TOTAL = TOTAL + VALUE; word 0: TOTAL0 = TOTAL0 + VALUE0 + carry\n\tgetA TOTAL1; getB VALUE1; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA TOTAL1; keepcarry CARRY # word 1\n\tgetA TOTAL2; getB VALUE2; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA TOTAL2; keepcarry CARRY # word 2\n\tgetA TOTAL3; getB VALUE3; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA TOTAL3  # word 3 (the top)\n\tlia 0; putA VALUE0; putA VALUE1; putA VALUE2; putA VALUE3    # VALUE = 0, all four words\n\tret\n\n# MULTIPLY: VALUE = VALUE * N, for N below 32,768.\n#     RESULT = 0; BIT = 1\n#     while BIT <= N:\n#         if (N and BIT) != 0: RESULT = RESULT + VALUE\n#         VALUE = VALUE + VALUE               # VALUE is now (what it was at the start) * 2 * BIT\n#         BIT = BIT + BIT\n#     VALUE = RESULT\n@ MULTIPLY\n\tlia 0; putA RESULT0; putA RESULT1; putA RESULT2; putA RESULT3 # RESULT = 0, all four words\n\tlia 1; putA BIT                                              # BIT = 1\n@ MULTIPLY_ROUND\n\tgetA N; getB BIT; sub                                        # A = N - BIT\n\tif_carry MULTIPLY_BIT                                        # N >= BIT: there may be more to add\n\tcopy RESULT0 VALUE0                                        # VALUE = RESULT; word 0 (the lowest)\n\tcopy RESULT1 VALUE1                                        # word 1\n\tcopy RESULT2 VALUE2                                        # word 2\n\tcopy RESULT3 VALUE3                                        # word 3 (the top)\n\tret\n@ MULTIPLY_BIT\n\tgetA N; getB BIT; and                                        # A = N and BIT\n\tlib 0                                                        # B = 0\n\tif_eq MULTIPLY_DOUBLE                                        # N does not have this power of two\n\tlia 0; putA CARRY                                            # CARRY = 0\n\tgetA RESULT0; getB VALUE0; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA RESULT0; keepcarry CARRY # RESULT = RESULT + VALUE; word 0: RESULT0 = RESULT0 + VALUE0 + carry\n\tgetA RESULT1; getB VALUE1; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA RESULT1; keepcarry CARRY # word 1\n\tgetA RESULT2; getB VALUE2; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA RESULT2; keepcarry CARRY # word 2\n\tgetA RESULT3; getB VALUE3; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA RESULT3 # word 3 (the top)\n@ MULTIPLY_DOUBLE\n\tlia 0; putA CARRY                                            # CARRY = 0\n\tgetA VALUE0; getB VALUE0; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE0; keepcarry CARRY # VALUE = VALUE + VALUE; word 0: VALUE0 = VALUE0 + VALUE0 + carry\n\tgetA VALUE1; getB VALUE1; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE1; keepcarry CARRY # word 1\n\tgetA VALUE2; getB VALUE2; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE2; keepcarry CARRY # word 2\n\tgetA VALUE3; getB VALUE3; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA VALUE3 # word 3 (the top)\n\tgetA BIT; getB BIT; sum; putA BIT                            # BIT = BIT + BIT\n\tgoto MULTIPLY_ROUND\n\n# SUBTRACT: DIFF = X - Y, and CARRY = 1 when X >= Y (0 when X < Y; DIFF is then of no use).\n# Done as X + (Y with every bit flipped) + 1, word by word from the lowest:\n#     CARRY = 1                                         # the \"+ 1\"\n#     for k in 0, 1, 2, 3:\n#         A = (0xFFFF - Yk) + Xk + CARRY                # at most 0x1FFFF\n#         DIFFk = the lower half of A; CARRY = the upper half of A\n# X and Y are left as they were.\n@ SUBTRACT\n\tlia 1; putA CARRY                                            # CARRY = 1\n\tgetA ALL_ONES; getB Y0; sub; getB X0; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA DIFF0; keepcarry CARRY # word 0: DIFF0 = (0xFFFF - Y0) + X0 + carry\n\tgetA ALL_ONES; getB Y1; sub; getB X1; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA DIFF1; keepcarry CARRY # word 1\n\tgetA ALL_ONES; getB Y2; sub; getB X2; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA DIFF2; keepcarry CARRY # word 2\n\tgetA ALL_ONES; getB Y3; sub; getB X3; sum; getB CARRY; sum; putA DIFF3; keepcarry CARRY # word 3: its carry is 1 when X >= Y\n\tret\n\n# ---- Powers of ten for the decimal digits: 10^14 down to 1, four words each, lowest first; then 0 ----\norigin 0x1E00\n0x4000; 0x107A; 0x5AF3; 0x0000    # 100000000000000\n0xA000; 0x4E72; 0x0918; 0x0000    # 10000000000000\n0x1000; 0xD4A5; 0x00E8; 0x0000    # 1000000000000\n0xE800; 0x4876; 0x0017; 0x0000    # 100000000000\n0xE400; 0x540B; 0x0002; 0x0000    # 10000000000\n0xCA00; 0x3B9A; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 1000000000\n0xE100; 0x05F5; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 100000000\n0x9680; 0x0098; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 10000000\n0x4240; 0x000F; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 1000000\n0x86A0; 0x0001; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 100000\n0x2710; 0x0000; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 10000\n0x03E8; 0x0000; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 1000\n0x0064; 0x0000; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 100\n0x000A; 0x0000; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 10\n0x0001; 0x0000; 0x0000; 0x0000    # 1\n0\n\n\n# ---- The worksheet: 4 rows of 3730 characters, then the row of signs ----\n# One word per character: a digit is its value, 0xFFF0 a space, 0xFFF1 +, 0xFFF2 *; 0xFFFF ends every row.\norigin 0x2000\n# row 1\n5; 1; 9; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 1; 3; 0xFFF0; 5; 2; 0xFFF0; 4; 4; 1; 0xFFF0; 1; 3; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0    # \"519  313 52 441 13  \"\n0xFFF0; 2; 1; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 7; 4; 0xFFF0; 5; 3; 3; 0xFFF0; 8; 5; 1; 9; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0    # \" 21   74 533 8519   \"\n9; 4; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 8; 1; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 4; 8; 0xFFF0; 9; 4; 0xFFF0; 5; 5; 2; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0    # \"94   81  48 94 552  \"\n7; 8; 3; 0xFFF0; 4; 5; 1; 0xFFF0; 1; 3; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 7; 8; 0xFFF0; 4; 1; 0xFFF0; 4; 9    # \"783 451 13  78 41 49\"\n9; 0xFFF0; 2; 9; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 5; 0xFFF0; 2; 6; 3; 0xFFF0; 7; 2; 7; 0xFFF0; 1; 8    # \"9 29    5 263 727 18\"\n0xFFF0; 7; 3; 0xFFF0; 1; 2; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 1; 0xFFF0; 7; 3; 9; 0xFFF0; 9; 1; 0xFFF0; 1; 6; 6    # \" 73 12  1 739 91 166\"\n5; 0xFFF0; 7; 9; 4; 0xFFF0; 7; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 1; 3; 5; 0xFFF0; 8; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 6; 6    # \"5 794 7  135 8   366\"\n0xFFF0; 7; 8; 0xFFF0; 5; 9; 8; 3; 0xFFF0; 7; 8; 1; 3; 0xFFF0; 1; 3; 9; 3; 0xFFF0; 9    # \" 78 5983 7813 1393 9\"\n5; 1; 6; 0xFFF0; 6; 3; 1; 0xFFF0; 5; 7; 8; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 4; 0xFFF0; 8; 9; 0xFFF0; 3    # \"516 631 578   4 89 3\"\n5; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 8; 0xFFF0; 1; 4; 0xFFF0; 9; 5; 0xFFF0; 4; 3; 1; 0xFFF0; 3; 1; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0    # \"5  38 14 95 431 31  \"\n0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 7; 0xFFF0; 7; 3; 0xFFF0; 2; 8; 0xFFF0; 7; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 8; 5; 0xFFF0; 6; 4    # \"  7 73 28 7   385 64\"\n2; 0xFFF0; 1; 9; 4; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 1; 0xFFF0; 5; 7; 6; 0xFFF0; 8; 7; 0xFFF0; 1; 5; 7    # \"2 194  31 576 87 157\"\n0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 3; 0xFFF0; 9; 6; 0xFFF0; 8; 3; 4; 7; 0xFFF0; 8; 7; 6; 0xFFF0; 8; 6; 6; 0xFFF0    # \"  3 96 8347 876 866 \"\n0xFFF0; 5; 3; 0xFFF0; 9; 5; 5; 0xFFF0; 9; 6; 2; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 5; 0xFFF0; 0xFFF0; 4; 7; 0xFFF0; 7    # \" 53 955 962  5  47 7\"\n2; 0xFFF0; 4; 3; 9; 1; 0xFFF0; 1; 6; 